  <section id="thinking">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-tag">ZONE_04</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Product Thinking Sample</h2>
      <div class="section-line"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="section-sub">Not tied to an employer — a problem I'd want to dig into if I were asked "what would you build?" for a logistics network.</p>

    <div class="flagship reveal" style="border-color:var(--teal);">
      <span class="flagship-tag" style="background:var(--teal);">✎ SELF-DIRECTED — HYPOTHETICAL</span>
      <div class="flagship-head">
        <div class="job-role">Cross-Warehouse Inventory Visibility</div>
        <div class="job-org">How I'd approach it for a multi-client 3PL network</div>
      </div>
      <div class="flagship-body">
        <div class="cs-grid">
          <div class="cs-block">
            <h4>Problem</h4>
            <p>In a multi-client 3PL, each warehouse tends to know its own stock but not what's happening two cities over. When a client asks "can you fulfill this order from anywhere in the network," the honest answer is often "let me call around and check" — that lag costs fulfillment speed and, eventually, client trust.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-block">
            <h4>Hypothesis</h4>
            <p>If operators had a single, near-real-time view of stock across all warehouses (not just their own), we could route orders to the nearest available inventory automatically — cutting fulfillment time and reducing "we're out of stock" answers that are actually just "we're out of stock <em>here</em>."</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-block">
            <h4>Discovery — what I'd ask first</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>How stale is "real-time" today — hourly batch sync, or truly live?</li>
              <li>Do warehouses use the same SKU taxonomy, or would this need a mapping layer first?</li>
              <li>Who actually makes the reroute call today — ops staff, or the client?</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-block">
            <h4>MVP scope</h4>
            <div class="moscow-grid" style="margin-top:0;">
              <div class="moscow-cell must"><span class="mtag">MUST</span><p>Live stock view across warehouses</p></div>
              <div class="moscow-cell should"><span class="mtag">SHOULD</span><p>Suggested reroute on stock-out</p></div>
              <div class="moscow-cell could"><span class="mtag">COULD</span><p>Auto-reroute with approval step</p></div>
              <div class="moscow-cell wont"><span class="mtag">WON'T (v1)</span><p>Fully automated rerouting</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tradeoff">
          <div class="ticon">⚖</div>
          <div>
            <h4>What I'd validate first</h4>
            <p>Before building anything, I'd want to know how often stock-outs actually happen when nearby inventory exists — if it's rare, this is a nice-to-have, not a roadmap priority. I'd pull that from existing order/fulfillment data before writing a single requirement.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

